 ## Background
-The concept of smooth minimum operators for SDFs has been popularized in the context of ray marching and procedural modeling. The polynomial variant (`smin`) is widely used in shader code for its simplicity [S4, unofficial]. The LogSumExp variant is derived from the soft-min function in optimization and machine learning [S2, unofficial]. These methods are commonly used in real-time graphics, particularly in demoscene productions and procedural generation tools [S3, unofficial].
